# Payloads, users.php and the sqlite database live here.
#
# This directory MUST NOT be readable over HTTP. On Apache this file handles it.
# On nginx you need a location block — see docs/install.md — or move data_dir
# outside the web root entirely, which is better on any host that lets you.
#
# Belt and braces: ndjson data files and users.php each begin with a PHP exit
# line, so their contents do not leak even if this file is ignored. The sqlite
# database cannot do that, which is why its filename carries a random suffix.
Require all denied
Options -Indexes
